      "name": "OMB M-26-14: Why federal agencies must fix asset visibility first",
      "description": "Office of Management and Budget (OMB) Director Russell Vought issued Memorandum M-26-14 , titled \u201cEnsuring Effective and Efficient Agency Logging and Network Visibility to Defend Against Evolving Cyber Threats.\u201d The directive rescinds M-21-31 and replaces it with a risk-based, prioritized logging framework designed to be both operationally achievable and aligned with today\u2019s threat landscape. Threat hunting, investigation, response, and forensics (THIRF): Centralized retrieval of historical log data to support post-compromise analysis and recovery.",
